  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nRadar is more active this afternoon with scattered showers and \nthunderstorms ongoing over the Victoria Crossroads. This activity \nwill continue to move inland and dissipate as daytime heating \ndiminishes this evening. The upper-level picture will begin to shift \nthis week as the Four Corners ridge migrates east, settling over SE \nCONUS by Friday. Subsidence aloft will stifle seabreeze convection \nthrough the week, but some mid-level energy may round the ridge on \nFriday and increase chances slightly. \n\nThe song remains the same regarding daily temperatures, with low to \nmid 90s near the coast, and triple digits west of Highway 281. \nIncreasing low-level moisture will raise dew points near 80 degrees \nalong the Coastal Bend, bringing heat indices up to 110-115 \nareawide. This corresponds to moderate to major HeatRisk (level 2-3) \nacross the CWA through Friday. A Heat Advisory may be needed on \nTuesday, and an issuance is likely on Wednesday. If working outside \nfor extended periods, remember to drink plenty of water and take \nfrequent breaks in shade or A/C.",
